The '''Office of the Inquisitorius''',<ref name="DOR VG" /> also known as the '''board room''',<ref name="Dark Times">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Obi-Wan Kenobi: The Complete Series|featurette=The Dark Times: Villains}}</ref> was an office with chairs, with the head seat being reserved for [[The Grand Inquisitor]]. It was a large room with a window that could see out [[Water|underwater]]. It also had a large strategy table in the middle of the room and was guarded by two [[stormtrooper]]s. Along the walls are dozens of [[Jedi]] [[lightsaber]]s and a few helmets that are traditionally worn by [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi younglings]]. In the meeting room, the [[Reva Sevander|Third Sister]] informed the other Inquisitors of her mission and that she has been put in charge of the [[hunt for Obi-Wan]] Kenobi, by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]]. She demanded that [[probe droid]]s be sent out to pinpoint [[Obi-Wan Kenobi|Obi-Wan's]] location, while the other inquisitors reluctantly agree to her temporary leadership, with the exception of the [[Fifth Brother]].<ref name="Part III" />

After Kenobi and the [[Hidden Path]] attacked the fortress to rescue [[princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], a furious Vader meet with the Third Sister, [[Fourth Sister]], and Fifth Brother. As Vader force choked the Third Sister Reva and threatened to kill her for the loss of Princess Leia, Reva revealed that she placed a tracker on their ship. She promised that the Empire will soon uncover the location of the Path network and Kenobi which convinced Vader decided to spare her.<ref name="Part IV">{{Kenobi|Part IV}}</ref>

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Office of the Inquisitorius first appeared in the [[Part III|third episode]] of the [[2022]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]''.<ref name="Part III" />

